------------------------------------------------------------------------
Oracle SDK repositories (data, not copied)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Stainless-generated SDKs pinned in oracles/manifest.yaml are cloned into
the gitignored oracles/cache/ at test time, and Ferrule's output is compared
against them. They are test data. No code from them is copied into this
repository or into generated SDKs, except the runtime and project files
credited above. Their licences, as GitHub reports them:
  Apache-2.0: OneBusAway/{python,js,go,java,kotlin,ruby}-sdk,
    groq/groq-python, lithic-com/lithic-python, perplexityai/perplexity-py,
    isaacus-dev/isaacus-{python,typescript}, lumalabs/lumaai-{python,node},
    plastic-labs/honcho-{python,node}-core,
    imagekit-developer/imagekit-{python,nodejs,go,java,ruby,php},
    knocklabs/knock-{python,node,go,java,ruby},
    knocklabs/knock-mgmt-{python,node,go},
    Papr-ai/papr-pythonSDK, Papr-ai/papr-TypescriptSDK
  MIT: anomalyco/opencode-sdk-{python,go}, browserbase/stagehand-python,
    ogx-ai/ogx-client-{python,typescript,go}
The config repositories they pair with are fetched the same way and are
never committed (oracles/README.md); some have no licence or a copyleft one.
